H2100.definition:
a primitive root;
to flow freely (as water), i.e. (specifically) to have a (sexual) flux; figuratively, to waste away; also to overflow
KJV: flow, gush out, have a (running) issue, pine away, run.

H2101.definition:
from H2100 (זוּב);
a seminal or menstrual flux
KJV: issue.

H2102.definition:
or (by permutation) זִיד; a primitive root;
to seethe; figuratively, to be insolent
KJV: be proud, deal proudly, presume, (come) presumptuously, sod.

H2103.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2102 (זוּד);
to be proud
KJV: in pride.

H2104.definition:
plural probably from the same as H2123 (זִיז); prominent;
Zuzites, an aboriginal tribe of Palestine
KJV: Zuzims.

H2105.definition:
of uncertain origin;
Zocheth, an Israelite
KJV: Zoheth.

H2106.definition:
apparently from the same root as H2099 (זִו) (in the sense of prominence);
an angle (as projecting), i.e. (by implication) a corner-column (or anta)
KJV: corner(stone).

H2107.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2151 (זָלַל));
probably to shake out, i.e. (by implication) to scatter profusely; figuratively, to treat lightly
KJV: lavish, despise.

H2108.definition:
from H2107 (זוּל);
probably scattering, i.e. removal; used adverbially, except
KJV: beside, but, only, save.

H2109.definition:
a primitive root;
perhaps properly, to be plump, i.e. (transitively) to nourish
KJV: feed.

H2110.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2109 (זוּן)
{perhaps properly, to be plump, i.e. (transitively) to nourish}
KJV: feed.

H2111.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to shake off, i.e. (figuratively) to agitate (as with fear)
KJV: move, tremble, vex.

H2112.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2111 (זוּעַ);
to shake (with fear)
KJV: tremble.

H2113.definition:
from H2111 (זוּעַ);
agitation, fear
KJV: be removed, trouble, vexation. Compare H2189 (זַעֲוָה).

H2114.definition:
a primitive root;
to turn aside (especially for lodging); hence to be aforeigner, strange, profane; specifically (active participle) to commit adultery
KJV: (come from) another (man, place), fanner, go away, (e-) strange(-r, thing, woman).

H2115.definition:
a primitive root (compare H6695 (צוֹק));
to press together, tighten
KJV: close, rush, thrust together.

H2116.definition:
from H2115 (זוּר);
trodden on
KJV: that which is crushed.

H2117.definition:
probably from the root of H2123 (זִיז); prominent;
Zaza, an Israelite
KJV: Zaza.

H2118.definition:
a primitive root;
to shove or displace
KJV: loose.

H2119.definition:
a primitive root;
to crawl; by implication, to fear
KJV: be afraid, serpent, worm.

H2120.definition:
feminine active participle of H2119 (זָחַל); crawling (i.e. serpent);
Zocheleth, a boundary stone in. Palestine
KJV: Zoheleth.

H2121.definition:
from H2102 (זוּד);
boiling of water, i.e. wave
KJV: proud.

H2122.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2099 (זִו);
(figuratively) cheerfulness
KJV: brightness, countenance.

H2123.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to be conspicuous;
fulness of the breast; also a moving creature
KJV: abundance, wild beast.

H2124.definition:
apparently from the same as H2123 (זִיז); prominence;
Ziza, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Ziza.

H2125.definition:
another form for H2124 (זִיזָא);
Zizah, an Israelite
KJV: Zizah.

H2126.definition:
from H2109 (זוּן); well-fed; or perhaps an orthographical error for H2124 (זִיזָא);
Zina, an Israelite
KJV: Zina.

H2127.definition:
from H2111 (זוּעַ); agitation;
Zia, an Israelite
KJV: Zia.

H2128.definition:
from the same as H2203 (זֶפֶת); flowing;
Ziph, the name of a place in Palestine; also of an Israelite
KJV: Ziph.

H2129.definition:
feminine of H2128 (זִיף); a flowing;
Ziphah, an Israelite
KJV: Ziphah.

H2130.definition:
patrial from H2128 (זִיף);
a Ziphite or inhabitant of Ziph
KJV: Ziphim, Ziphite.

H2131.definition:
(Isaiah 50: (feminine); and זִק; or זֵק; from H2187 (זָנַק);
properly, what leaps forth, i.e. flash of fire, or a burning arrow; also (from the original sense of the root) a bond
KJV: chain, fetter, firebrand, spark.

H2132.definition:
probably from an unused root (akin to H2099 (זִו));
an olive (as yielding illuminating oil), the tree, the branch or the berry
KJV: olive (tree, -yard), Olivet.

H2133.definition:
from H2132 (זַיִת); olive grove;
Zethan, an Israelite
KJV: Zethan.

H2134.definition:
from H2141 (זָכַךְ);
clear
KJV: clean, pure.

H2135.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2141 (זָכַךְ));
to be translucent; figuratively, to be innocent
KJV: be (make) clean, cleanse, be clear, count pure.

H2136.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2135 (זָכָה);
purity
KJV: innocency.

H2137.definition:
from H2135 (זָכָה);
properly, transparency, i.e. glass
KJV: crystal.

H2138.definition:
properly, passive participle of H2142 (זָכַר), but used for H2145 (זָכָר);
a male (of man or animals)
KJV: males, men-children.

H2139.definition:
from H2142 (זָכַר); mindful;
Zakkur, the name of seven Israelites
KJV: Zaccur, Zacchur.

H2140.definition:
from H2141 (זָכַךְ); pure;
Zakkai, an Israelite
KJV: Zaccai.

H2141.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2135 (זָכָה));
to be transparent or clean (phys. or morally)
KJV: be (make) clean, be pure(-r).

H2143.definition:
or זֶכֶר; from H2142 (זָכַר);
a memento, abstractly recollection (rarely if ever); by implication, commemoration
KJV: memorial, memory, remembrance, scent.

H2144.definition:
the same as H2143 (זֵכֶר);
Zeker, an Israelite
KJV: Zeker.

H2145.definition:
from H2142 (זָכַר);
properly, remembered, i.e. a male (of man or animals, as being the most noteworthy sex)
KJV: [idiom] him, male, man(child, -kind).

H2146.definition:
from H2142 (זָכַר);
a memento (or memorable thing, day or writing)
KJV: memorial, record.

H2147.definition:
from H2142 (זָכַר); memorable;
Zicri, the name of twelve Israelites
KJV: Zichri.

H2148.definition:
or זְכַרְיָהוּ; from H2142 (זָכַר) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has remembered;
Zecarjah, the name of twenty-nine Israelites
KJV: Zachariah, Zechariah.

H2149.definition:
from H2151 (זָלַל);
properly, a shaking, i.e. perhaps a tempest
KJV: vilest.

H2150.definition:
by reduplication from H2151 (זָלַל);
tremulous, i.e. a twig
KJV: sprig.

H2151.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2107 (זוּל));
to shake (as in the wind), i.e. to quake; figuratively, to be loose morally, worthless or prodigal
KJV: blow down, glutton, riotous (eater), vile.

H2152.definition:
or זִלְעָפָהxlit zilʻâphâph corrected to zilʻâphâh; from H2196 (זָעַף);
a glow (of wind or anger); also a famine (as consuming)
KJV: horrible, horror, terrible.

H2153.definition:
; from an unused root apparently meaning to trickle, as myrrh; fragrant dropping;
Zilpah, Leah's maid
KJV: Zilpah.

H2154.definition:
or זַמָּה; from H2161 (זָמַם);
a plan, especially a bad one
KJV: heinous crime, lewd(-ly, -ness), mischief, purpose, thought, wicked (device, mind, -ness).

H2155.definition:
the same as H2154 (זִמָּה);
Zimmah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Zimmah.

H2156.definition:
or זְמֹרָה (feminine); and זְמֹר (masculine); from H2168 (זָמַר);
a twig (as pruned)
KJV: vine, branch, slip.

H2157.definition:
from H2161 (זָמַם); intriguing;
a Zamzumite, or native tribe of Palestine
KJV: Zamzummim.

H2158.definition:
or זָמִר; and (feminine) זְמִרָה; from H2167 (זָמַר);
a song to be accompanied with instrumental music
KJV: psalm(-ist), singing, song.

H2159.definition:
from H2168 (זָמַר);
a twig (as pruned)
KJV: branch.

H2160.definition:
feminine of H2158 (זָמִיר); song;
Zemirah, an Israelite
KJV: Zemira.

H2161.definition:
a primitive root;
to plan, usually in a bad sense
KJV: consider, devise, imagine, plot, purpose, think (evil).

H2162.definition:
from H2161 (זָמַם);
a plot
KJV: wicked device.

H2163.definition:
a primitive root;
to fix (a time)
KJV: appoint.

H2164.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2163 (זָמַן);
to agree (on a time and place)
KJV: prepare.

H2165.definition:
from H2163 (זָמַן);
an appointed occasion
KJV: season, time.

H2166.definition:
(Aramaic) from H2165 (זְמָן); the same as H2165 (זְמָן)
{an appointed occasion}
KJV: season, time.

H2168.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2167 (זָמַר), H5568 (סָמַר), H6785 (צֶמֶר));
to trim (a vine)
KJV: prune.

H2169.definition:
apparently from H2167 (זָמַר) or H2168 (זָמַר);
a gazelle (from its lightly touching the ground)
KJV: chamois.

H2170.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2167 (זָמַר);
instrumental music
KJV: musick.

H2171.definition:
(Aramaic) from the same as H2170 (זְמָר);
an instrumental musician
KJV: singer.

H2172.definition:
from H2167 (זָמַר);
a musical piece or song to be accompanied by an instrument
KJV: melody, psalm.

H2173.definition:
from H2168 (זָמַר);
pruned (i.e. choice) fruit
KJV: best fruit.

H2174.definition:
from H2167 (זָמַר); musical;
Zimri, the name of five Israelites, and of an Arabian tribe
KJV: Zimri.

H2175.definition:
from H2167 (זָמַר); musical;
Zimran, a son of Abraham by Keturah
KJV: Zimran.

H2176.definition:
from H2167 (זָמַר);
instrumental music; by implication, praise
KJV: song.

H2177.definition:
from H2109 (זוּן);
properly, nourished (or fully developed), i.e. a form or sort
KJV: divers kinds, [idiom] all manner of store.

H2178.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2177 (זַן);
sort
KJV: kind.

H2179.definition:
a primitive root meaning to wag; used only as a denominative from H2180 (זָנָב);
to curtail, i.e. cut off the rear
KJV: smite the hindmost.

H2180.definition:
from H2179 (זָנַב) (in the original sense of flapping);
the tail (literally or figuratively)
KJV: tail.

H2181.definition:
a primitive root (highly-fed and therefore wanton);
to commit adultery (usually of the female, and less often of simple fornication, rarely of involuntary ravishment); figuratively, to commit idolatry (the Jewish people being regarded as the spouse of Jehovah)
KJV: (cause to) commit fornication, [idiom] continually, [idiom] great, (be an, play the) harlot, (cause to be, play the) whore, (commit, fall to) whoredom, (cause to) go a-whoring, whorish.

H2182.definition:
from H2186 (זָנַח); rejected;
Zanoach, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV: Zanoah.

H2183.definition:
from H2181 (זָנָה);
adultery; figuratively, idolatry
KJV: whoredom.

H2184.definition:
from H2181 (זָנָה);
adultery, i.e. (figuratively) infidelity, idolatry
KJV: whoredom.

H2185.definition:
regarded by some as if from H2109 (זוּן) or an unused root, and applied to military equipments; but evidently the feminine plural active participle of H2181 (זָנָה);
harlots
KJV: armour.

H2187.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to draw together the feet (as an animal about to dart upon its prey), i.e. to spring forward
KJV: leap.

H2188.definition:
from H2111 (זוּעַ) (in the sense of H3154 (יֶזַע));
perspiration
KJV: sweat.

H2189.definition:
by transposition for H2113 (זְוָעָה);
agitation, maltreatment
KJV: [idiom] removed, trouble.

H2190.definition:
from H2111 (זוּעַ); disquiet;
Zaavan, an Idumaean
KJV: Zaavan.

H2191.definition:
from an unused root (akin (by permutation) to H6819 (צָעַר)), meaning to dwindle;
small
KJV: little.

H2192.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2191 (זְעֵיר)xlit zeʻêyr corrected to zᵉʻêyr
{small}
KJV: little.

H2193.definition:
a primitive root;
to extinguish
KJV: be extinct.

H2194.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to foam at the mouth, i.e. to be enraged
KJV: abhor, abominable, (be) angry, defy, (have) indignation.

H2195.definition:
from H2194 (זָעַם);
strictly froth at the mouth, i.e. (figuratively) fury (especially of God's displeasure with sin)
KJV: angry, indignation, rage.

H2196.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to boil up, i.e. (figuratively) to be peevish or angry
KJV: fret, sad, worse liking, be wroth.

H2197.definition:
from H2196 (זָעַף);
anger
KJV: indignation, rage(-ing), wrath.

H2199.definition:
a primitive root;
to shriek (from anguish or danger); by analogy, (as a herald) to announce or convene publicly
KJV: assemble, call (together), (make a) cry (out), come with such a company, gather (together), cause to be proclaimed.
